WEBVTT

00:35.582 --> 00:36.891
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

00:36.892 --> 00:39.155
Our top story tonight,
scientists at NASA

00:39.203 --> 00:40.968
have made a fascinating
new discovery:

00:41.139 --> 00:44.011
the first directly observable
instance of a black hole,

00:44.012 --> 00:46.578
which appears to be located
just outside our solar system.

00:46.948 --> 00:48.822
Tricia Takanawa has the story.

00:48.823 --> 00:52.067
Tom, I'm standing here
with Stephen Hawking,

00:52.068 --> 00:54.004
the first white man I've ever met

00:54.005 --> 00:55.871
who knows math better than me.

00:56.255 --> 00:59.062
Mr. Hawking, what does the
discovery of this black hole

00:59.063 --> 01:00.863
mean to you and your research?

01:01.561 --> 01:02.810
I am overjoyed.

01:02.811 --> 01:06.479
This is the crowning
achievement of my career.

01:06.557 --> 01:09.759
It validates the
work of a lifetime.

01:10.056 --> 01:11.551
It certainly does.

01:11.552 --> 01:12.819
Back to you, Tom.

01:13.179 --> 01:14.212
All right, we're clear.

01:14.615 --> 01:15.423
I'm telling you, man,

01:15.424 --> 01:16.485
this shtick is getting so old.

01:16.486 --> 01:17.786
That chair smells, dude.

01:17.798 --> 01:19.064
Hey, Steve, surf's up!

01:19.546 --> 01:20.513
All right!

01:20.545 --> 01:22.112
See you, bitch!

01:22.855 --> 01:24.491
Everyone, guess what.

01:24.981 --> 01:25.543
What?

01:25.544 --> 01:27.915
I have been selected.

01:28.541 --> 01:29.288
For what?

01:29.289 --> 01:30.413
Oh, nothing too important,
just jury duty!

01:30.414 --> 01:32.049
They have summoned me.

01:33.661 --> 01:35.720
I am part of an elite
group of individuals

01:35.721 --> 01:37.223
deemed intelligent enough to decide

01:37.224 --> 01:39.090
the fate of a fellow citizen.

01:42.653 --> 01:44.779
Ah, the amused laughter
of the envious.

01:44.780 --> 01:46.838
You know, they don't just
pick anybody for this job.

01:46.839 --> 01:47.973
Yeah, they do.

01:48.587 --> 01:50.460
Brian, perhaps I have
not made myself clear.

01:50.461 --> 01:53.730
I have been entrusted to
pass judgment upon others.

01:53.895 --> 01:56.565
Everybody gets called for jury duty,
you stupid idiot!

01:56.893 --> 01:58.077
I've been called!

01:58.078 --> 01:59.390
The only reason you've
never been called

01:59.391 --> 02:01.202
is that they use the
voter registration list,

02:01.203 --> 02:03.273
and this past election is the
first time you ever voted.

02:03.575 --> 02:04.742
I voted before.

02:04.761 --> 02:06.663
I stuffed the ballot
box at the Oscars.

02:07.074 --> 02:10.632
And the nominees for Best
Actor in a Leading Role are:

02:10.633 --> 02:13.601
<i>Grover, Bluto from Popeye,</i>

02:13.632 --> 02:15.066
a red guy, a boob

02:15.067 --> 02:16.801
and Daniel Day Lewis.

02:17.753 --> 02:19.989
And the Oscar goes to...

02:20.124 --> 02:21.158
a red guy!

02:26.306 --> 02:27.672
Wait a second. Y-You're saying that

02:27.931 --> 02:30.304
everyone is asked to do jury duty?

02:30.305 --> 02:31.372
Yes, Peter.

02:31.429 --> 02:33.864
So then, I'm not special?

02:33.926 --> 02:36.111
Everyone's special, Peter.

02:36.112 --> 02:37.170
Rock Drummer Tommy Lee?!

02:37.171 --> 02:39.573
And if your wife ever tells
you that you're not special,

02:40.233 --> 02:42.484
punch her really hard
right in her hepatitis.

02:42.485 --> 02:44.255
Thanks, Rock Drummer Tommy Lee!

02:44.666 --> 02:46.102
Hey, and you know
what else is cool?

02:46.103 --> 02:48.171
Having sex with sunglasses on.

02:48.290 --> 02:50.527
I've got a lot of
things to try now!

02:54.909 --> 02:56.722
I don't want to go to jury duty.

02:56.723 --> 02:58.406
Turns out it's not a special
honor at all. It's lame.

02:58.407 --> 03:00.477
And the worst part is,
they try and trick you

03:01.278 --> 03:03.348
into getting excited by
putting "duty" in the title.

03:03.402 --> 03:04.803
So, you were excited
when you thought

03:04.839 --> 03:06.441
there was fecal matter involved?

03:06.528 --> 03:07.829
What the hell is fecal matter?

03:07.903 --> 03:08.836
Waste. Huh?

03:08.898 --> 03:09.584
Doody. Ha-ha!

03:09.585 --> 03:11.953
Peter, jury duty is an
important cornerstone

03:12.270 --> 03:13.571
in our democratic society.

03:14.020 --> 03:16.021
Yeah, that's what separates
us from the monkeys.

03:16.204 --> 03:18.407
That and the armed
guards at the zoo.

03:18.454 --> 03:21.057
Man, they got some sexy
monkeys down there.

03:21.075 --> 03:22.843
I don't care,
jury duty sounds boring.

03:23.201 --> 03:24.635
I'm gonna get myself kicked out.

03:24.636 --> 03:26.538
Just like I got kicked
out of Coldplay.

03:27.695 --> 03:29.254
Guys, guys, I got an idea!

03:29.255 --> 03:32.360
How 'bout we do a song
that's not whiny bull crap?

03:36.002 --> 03:37.440
All right, ladies and gentlemen.

03:37.441 --> 03:39.936
We're gonna ask you a series
of questions to determine

03:39.937 --> 03:42.205
whether or not you can
be impartial jurors.

03:42.439 --> 03:45.042
First off, do any of
you have any prejudices

03:45.120 --> 03:46.855
you feel the court should know of?

03:47.245 --> 03:48.181
Yes, you sir.

03:48.182 --> 03:49.450
Ants. I hate ants.

03:50.053 --> 03:50.552
What?

03:50.553 --> 03:51.426
That's right, you heard me.

03:51.427 --> 03:52.563
I'm an ant hater.

03:52.613 --> 03:54.716
Just like my daddy and
his daddy before him.

03:54.926 --> 03:56.673
So, if this is an ant trial,
forget it.

03:56.674 --> 03:58.376
No way I'm gonna be fair.

03:58.611 --> 04:00.947
Always making those
cocky little hills.

04:00.984 --> 04:03.587
Moving around all
single file and stupid.

04:03.668 --> 04:06.972
All ganging up and walking my
pie off the picnic blanket.

04:12.035 --> 04:14.706
'Twas my pie gone missing!

04:15.033 --> 04:16.434
Sir, this is not an ant trial.

04:16.470 --> 04:17.156
Oh.

04:17.157 --> 04:18.592
Is there anything else
we should know about?

04:19.031 --> 04:20.031
Oh, have you not heard?

04:20.091 --> 04:20.843
Heard what?

04:20.844 --> 04:22.279
? A well-a-bird-bird-bird ?

04:22.280 --> 04:24.584
? B-Bird's the word,
a well-a-bird-bird-bird ?

04:24.714 --> 04:25.650
? B-Bird's the word, a well-a... ?

04:25.651 --> 04:28.088
All right, now the prosecution
is about to show you

04:30.645 --> 04:32.114
items pertinent to this case

04:32.331 --> 04:33.518
that have been entered
into evidence.

04:33.519 --> 04:36.391
It is vitally important that
you look but don't touch,

04:36.519 --> 04:38.622
as any fingerprints
could contaminate them.

04:38.828 --> 04:40.998
Exhibit A, one bloody Slinky.

04:41.327 --> 04:42.014
Oh.

04:42.015 --> 04:42.951
Exhibit B,

04:42.952 --> 04:44.788
one semen-covered View-Master.

04:44.885 --> 04:45.987
Oh!

04:46.009 --> 04:47.778
With the reel of the Grand Canyon.

04:48.132 --> 04:49.380
Oh!

04:49.381 --> 04:51.583
And a blood-splattered Mr.
Potato Head.

04:51.754 --> 04:53.022
Oh!

04:53.129 --> 04:54.696
And these socks you really need.

04:55.627 --> 04:57.029
Oh!

04:58.500 --> 05:01.272
All right, everyone, we're going
to take a ten-minute recess.

05:01.310 --> 05:03.681
I would like to remind members
of the jury that you are

05:03.682 --> 05:06.687
forbidden to discuss details of
the case outside the courtroom.

05:11.238 --> 05:12.737
Hey, how about this trial, huh?

05:12.738 --> 05:13.669
And all its details.

05:13.738 --> 05:14.735
Let's discuss them.

05:14.861 --> 05:16.049
He said not to!

05:16.050 --> 05:17.484
Aw, hey, you know how
the judge told us

05:17.485 --> 05:18.783
not to make up our
minds beforehand?

05:18.920 --> 05:19.952
Let's make up our minds.

05:20.108 --> 05:21.073
Griffin, shut up!

05:21.106 --> 05:22.166
Hey, I know the judge said

05:22.167 --> 05:23.866
not to run in the hall,
but check this out!

05:30.223 --> 05:31.846
Griffin! Knock it off!

05:31.847 --> 05:33.595
Hey, come on, Judge,
tell us the answer.

05:33.596 --> 05:35.230
The Mexican guy did it, right?

05:39.032 --> 05:42.169
<i>We now return to How Henry
Kissinger Met Your Mother.</i>

05:42.466 --> 05:45.024
I was walking with my professor

05:45.025 --> 05:47.528
when I saw this woman who was...

06:03.386 --> 06:04.571
Stewie, can you please move?

06:04.572 --> 06:05.444
You're blocking the TV.

06:05.445 --> 06:07.148
No! And I'll thank
you to quiet down.

06:07.257 --> 06:08.592
I'm playing action figures.

06:08.820 --> 06:10.654
Prepare to be bested on
the battlefield, Lion-O.

06:11.006 --> 06:12.241
Oh, I don't think so, He-Man.

06:12.940 --> 06:13.314
Ow!

06:13.315 --> 06:14.626
Oh, I'm sorry,
did I punch you too hard?

06:14.627 --> 06:16.061
Yes, I suppose you don't
know your own strength.

06:16.501 --> 06:17.376
I mean, look at your muscles.

06:17.377 --> 06:19.111
Oh, stop it, you're the
one with the sick abs.

06:19.749 --> 06:22.386
God, my mouth is watering
just looking at you.

06:22.683 --> 06:23.618
Yeah, that's right.

06:23.619 --> 06:25.856
You buy your kids
ridiculously homoerotic dolls

06:26.057 --> 06:27.240
and then ask what happened?

06:27.241 --> 06:29.745
Yep. Your gay son is on you, buddy.

06:29.990 --> 06:31.624
Explain that to your god.

06:32.112 --> 06:34.110
Off to another day of
jury duty, sweetie?

06:34.111 --> 06:35.361
Yeah, and it sucks.

06:35.362 --> 06:37.331
Even the vending machines
are out of order.

06:40.544 --> 06:42.813
I don't want to go back
to stupid jury duty.

06:43.043 --> 06:45.038
There's got to be some
way I can get out of it.

06:45.039 --> 06:47.209
This is Tom Tucker with
some breaking news.

06:47.227 --> 06:49.161
NASA has made the
alarming announcement

06:49.162 --> 06:50.696
that the newly
discovered black hole

06:50.913 --> 06:53.597
at the edge of our solar
system appears to be expanding.

06:53.598 --> 06:55.781
Neptune and Pluto have
already been consumed,

06:55.782 --> 06:57.717
and scientists estimate
that the event horizon

06:57.718 --> 06:59.218
will reach Earth by tomorrow.

06:59.405 --> 07:00.340
That's right, Tom.

07:00.341 --> 07:01.676
Which means th all life on Earth

07:01.840 --> 07:03.842
will be destroyed within 24 hours.

07:04.526 --> 07:06.209
Oh, my God!

07:06.210 --> 07:08.458
Mom, is, is this for real?

07:08.459 --> 07:10.194
Well, it sure looks
that way, sweetie.

07:10.584 --> 07:12.954
It's the end of the world!

07:13.017 --> 07:14.518
Holy crap!

07:18.327 --> 07:20.595
Seems like I've run
out of waiting time.

07:25.816 --> 07:27.500
...but it looks like
Nicole Ritchie's baby

07:27.501 --> 07:29.170
is gonna be just fine.

07:29.251 --> 07:31.559
Also in the news,
the doomsday clock is ticking

07:31.560 --> 07:33.930
with less than 19 hours
to go before our planet

07:33.933 --> 07:36.270
is consumed by an
expanding black hole.

07:36.557 --> 07:39.365
As Americans everywhere face
their last day on Earth,

07:39.366 --> 07:41.402
one can only imagine how
they're spending it.

07:43.861 --> 07:44.485
Hey, Mort.

07:44.486 --> 07:45.858
Now that the end of
the world is here,

07:45.859 --> 07:48.097
I just wanted to say
no hard feelings, huh?

07:49.422 --> 07:50.106
Ow!

07:50.107 --> 07:51.106
Psych! Ha-ha!

07:51.107 --> 07:52.919
Embedded in the hand.

07:52.920 --> 07:54.421
Have fun where you're going.

07:55.790 --> 07:57.539
Well, it's become clear,

07:57.540 --> 07:59.412
the only way to avert this disaster

07:59.413 --> 08:02.719
is by writing a strongly-worded
letter to the black hole.

08:03.161 --> 08:04.470
"Dear space.

08:04.471 --> 08:07.143
"Well, you're just full
of surprises, aren't you?

08:07.281 --> 08:10.320
"You think you're so good
'cause you went to Choate.

08:10.470 --> 08:11.871
"Well, you're not gonna be so tough

08:12.026 --> 08:13.650
"when I put a fish bowl on my head

08:13.651 --> 08:16.755
and a rocket pack on my back and
come up there and punch you."

08:26.128 --> 08:27.961
Take that, Orion!

08:30.936 --> 08:31.685
That's rig.

08:31.686 --> 08:34.619
All you are is a failed
production company.

08:36.743 --> 08:38.311
Joe, Joe, you got to help me.

08:38.371 --> 08:39.555
You got to help me get laid!

08:39.556 --> 08:40.690
What are you talking about,
Quagmire?

08:40.929 --> 08:41.963
I got to get laid!

08:42.117 --> 08:42.990
You got to help me get laid!

08:42.991 --> 08:44.175
I've never had sex!

08:44.176 --> 08:46.045
What do you mean?
You've had sex a million times.

08:46.176 --> 08:47.209
Aw, that's all bluster.

08:47.298 --> 08:48.734
I just talk big for the fellas.

08:48.923 --> 08:50.389
I'm a virgin, Joe!

08:50.421 --> 08:51.823
I don't want to die a virgin!

08:52.047 --> 08:53.448
Help me, please!

08:53.484 --> 08:55.416
Let me have sex with Bonnie!

08:56.542 --> 08:58.043
I guess so.

08:58.044 --> 09:00.779
For my friend,
on our last day on Earth.

09:01.039 --> 09:03.175
You're a good man, Joe Swanson.

09:04.410 --> 09:05.658
How was your first time?

09:05.659 --> 09:07.159
Ah, I've had sex lots of times.

09:07.160 --> 09:08.327
I just wanted to have it again!

09:11.282 --> 09:12.385
Screw you!

09:12.842 --> 09:15.028
Who else but Quagmire?

09:15.029 --> 09:16.837
Well, Diane, now that
our time is almost up,

09:16.838 --> 09:18.941
just to lighten the mood,
we introduce a new feature

09:19.149 --> 09:21.185
called Tom's Crank Calls.

09:21.396 --> 09:23.831
Let's dial that number, shall we?

09:24.146 --> 09:26.142
Hello, is this Megan Fox?

09:26.143 --> 09:28.044
I will kill you, do you understand?

09:28.080 --> 09:29.648
If I can't have you, no one can.

09:29.703 --> 09:30.637
I will kill you.

09:30.702 --> 09:32.672
This is Tom Tucker.

09:32.888 --> 09:34.456
<i>Well, I know who you are.</i>

09:35.698 --> 09:38.234
It's fun to see how people
react when they're on the spot.

09:38.758 --> 09:40.758
Look, since these
are our final hours,

09:40.759 --> 09:42.568
I want you kids to know how much

09:42.569 --> 09:44.072
your father and I love you

09:44.193 --> 09:46.329
and how important
this family is to us.

09:46.568 --> 09:47.869
Oh, I'm scared.

09:47.876 --> 09:49.644
I wonder what it's like to die.

09:49.749 --> 09:52.497
I don't know, but from the
look in a stray cat's eyes

09:52.498 --> 09:54.060
when you're pushing
on its windpipe,

09:54.061 --> 09:55.363
I think it's pretty terrifying.

09:55.871 --> 09:57.243
Like, panicky.

09:57.244 --> 09:59.214
Hey, Brian, what do you
think is gonna happ--

09:59.617 --> 10:00.679
What was that--

10:00.680 --> 10:01.779
You were praying.

10:01.802 --> 10:02.936
Come on, no, I wasn't.

10:03.116 --> 10:03.987
Yes, you were.

10:03.988 --> 10:05.355
You were praying, I saw!

10:05.550 --> 10:06.750
No, man, it was a joke!

10:06.800 --> 10:07.800
You were praying!

10:07.986 --> 10:09.732
It was a goof!
I was goofing on you!

10:09.733 --> 10:12.170
You're, you're,
you're disingenuous.

10:14.232 --> 10:15.103
Hello, everybody.

10:15.104 --> 10:16.939
This is Montecore. He's my lion.

10:17.164 --> 10:18.165
I have a lion now.

10:19.601 --> 10:20.835
Peter, what the hell?!

10:21.037 --> 10:22.286
You know, I went to
the zoo last week

10:22.287 --> 10:24.191
and asked if I could do it,
and they told me to scram.

10:24.227 --> 10:25.261
Went to the zoo this morning

10:25.347 --> 10:26.682
with a shotgun and
now I have a lion.

10:27.157 --> 10:28.793
Does it bite? Of course
it bites, it's a lion.

10:29.221 --> 10:30.654
Peter, get off the lion.

10:30.655 --> 10:32.715
We should spend some time
together as a family.

10:32.716 --> 10:33.918
I don't think so, Lois.

10:34.279 --> 10:35.711
But the world is ending.

10:35.712 --> 10:37.215
We should be spending
these final hours

10:37.276 --> 10:38.944
with the people we love most.

10:39.025 --> 10:41.227
Lois, a day ago,
I was stuck on jury duty.

10:41.333 --> 10:43.803
Today, I have a golden ticket
to do whatever the hell I want.

10:44.084 --> 10:45.017
I feel like an old guy

10:45.018 --> 10:46.991
who's reliving his
youthful shenanigans.

10:47.454 --> 10:49.451
Tell me about when you
were young, Grandpa.

10:49.452 --> 10:51.889
Oh, sonny, those were crazy times.

10:52.013 --> 10:54.012
My friends and I
were out of control.

10:54.013 --> 10:56.617
We used to give each other
wet-willies and funny arms.

10:56.697 --> 10:59.668
We'd play dandy-balls and
legs-a-spread and penis-butt.

11:00.135 --> 11:01.568
Sounds kind of gay, Grandpa.

11:01.569 --> 11:03.438
It was gay. Everyone was.

11:03.629 --> 11:05.966
But, back then,
we were called pole-fancies.

11:06.065 --> 11:07.625
It was real, good old-fashioned

11:07.626 --> 11:10.495
"grab the nearest tree and
hold on for dear life" gay,

11:10.561 --> 11:13.433
not today's fancy, featherbed,
thread-count gay.

11:13.495 --> 11:14.797
People got hurt back then!

11:15.184 --> 11:15.930
That's gay.

11:15.931 --> 11:16.965
Yeah, it was pretty gay.

11:20.930 --> 11:22.426
What the hell are you
doing with a musket?

11:22.427 --> 11:23.425
Last day on Earth.

11:23.426 --> 11:25.795
I've always wanted to save
a Native American family

11:25.801 --> 11:27.102
from rapacious cavalrymen.

11:35.230 --> 11:37.865
<i>Yeah... this one'll do nicely.</i>

11:39.726 --> 11:41.729
Let her go.

11:43.347 --> 11:46.481
You don't have to be
afraid of him anymore.

11:49.470 --> 11:52.027
Stay with us as the countdown
to Doomsday continues

11:52.028 --> 11:53.895
with just six more hours to go.

11:54.216 --> 11:56.027
The only thing that's
nice about this is

11:56.028 --> 11:57.462
even though it's a Tuesday,

11:57.463 --> 11:59.432
it feels kinda like it's a Friday.

12:00.709 --> 12:02.019
Peter, where are you going?

12:02.020 --> 12:04.018
Last day on Earth,
last chance to do this.

12:04.019 --> 12:05.266
I'm gonna find a black neighborhood

12:05.267 --> 12:06.202
and see what happens

12:06.203 --> 12:07.571
if I yell the you-know-what word.

12:11.575 --> 12:13.810
They respected me for saying it.

12:18.260 --> 12:18.507
Well, ladies and gentlemen,
this is it,

12:18.508 --> 12:19.841
our final minutes.

12:21.007 --> 12:22.712
Any moment now,
the Earth will be sucked

12:22.878 --> 12:24.252
into the gaping maw
of the black hole.

12:24.253 --> 12:26.391
We here at Channel Five
would like to leave you

12:26.813 --> 12:28.982
with some highlights of
mankind's brief existence,

12:29.562 --> 12:31.248
like the Battle of Hastings.

12:31.249 --> 12:33.689
Guys, if we win this,
we get Hastings!

12:34.245 --> 12:35.368
Yeah, let's do it!

12:35.369 --> 12:36.056
Let's go!

12:36.057 --> 12:37.693
All right, Hastings!

12:37.868 --> 12:39.404
The Ottoman Empire.

12:39.554 --> 12:40.864
Ah, I could get used to this.

12:40.865 --> 12:41.803
You know what?

12:41.804 --> 12:44.203
This is what I want our
empire to be about.

12:44.490 --> 12:46.592
The first television broadcast.

12:59.724 --> 13:01.474
And with only 30 seconds to go,

13:01.475 --> 13:02.944
we thank you for
choosing Channel Five

13:03.035 --> 13:04.302
as your Armageddon network.

13:04.595 --> 13:06.064
Mom, where's Dad?!

13:06.096 --> 13:07.531
I don't know, Chris.

13:07.533 --> 13:08.529
Sorry I'm late, guys.

13:08.530 --> 13:09.798
Peter, where have you been?!

13:10.154 --> 13:11.790
Look, you try scheduling
a haircut today.

13:11.902 --> 13:13.526
You know, you'd think
you'd wanna spend

13:13.527 --> 13:15.064
your last day on Earth
with your family!

13:15.338 --> 13:16.371
Hey, I'm here, aren't I?

13:16.400 --> 13:18.209
With only seconds left!

13:18.210 --> 13:19.544
Don't you love me?!

13:19.772 --> 13:20.895
Of course I love you, Lois!

13:20.896 --> 13:22.899
You're the most important
person in the world to me!

13:23.582 --> 13:24.704
You promise?

13:24.705 --> 13:25.505
I promise!

13:27.453 --> 13:27.890
Ten, nine, eight...

13:27.891 --> 13:29.390
I just hate bein' around the kids.

13:31.701 --> 13:32.468
What?!

13:32.637 --> 13:34.135
...six, five,

13:34.136 --> 13:35.270
Sorry, I just thought I'd be honest

13:35.571 --> 13:36.506
since we're gonna die.

13:36.576 --> 13:39.568
...three, two, one.

13:39.569 --> 13:41.237
April Fools!

13:41.942 --> 13:42.755
What?!

13:42.756 --> 13:44.123
You gotta be kiddin' me!

13:44.376 --> 13:45.344
We're not gonna die?!

13:45.563 --> 13:47.563
No, we're not gonna die!

13:51.498 --> 13:53.600
Wait, what did Dad just say?

13:56.939 --> 13:57.939
Yes, April Fools!

13:58.561 --> 13:59.863
We at Channel Five News concocted

14:00.433 --> 14:02.305
the whole black hole story
as part of our commitment

14:02.306 --> 14:03.974
to being festive
around the holidays.

14:03.994 --> 14:06.679
And with only 87 suicides
and widespread looting,

14:06.680 --> 14:09.518
we think this was a pretty
successful practical joke.

14:10.238 --> 14:12.300
You dicks!

14:12.301 --> 14:14.135
Hey, how do ya like that, Lois?

14:14.236 --> 14:15.233
We're gonna live!

14:15.234 --> 14:17.168
Peter, what did you
mean by what you said,

14:17.169 --> 14:19.538
you hate bein' around the kids?

14:19.667 --> 14:21.103
Yeah, Dad, what did you mean?

14:21.104 --> 14:22.070
Don't you like us?

14:22.418 --> 14:23.351
Yeah, what gives?

14:23.479 --> 14:24.665
Well... Oh, come on.

14:24.666 --> 14:26.467
I-I didn't mean that.
I was just jokin' around.

14:26.787 --> 14:27.955
Hey, gimme a big hug.

14:28.161 --> 14:30.397
How about a big hug for old Dad?

14:30.722 --> 14:32.158
Kids, why don't you go upstairs

14:32.159 --> 14:33.793
so your father and I can talk.

14:34.033 --> 14:35.801
Yeah, come on, Meg and Chris.

14:35.843 --> 14:37.077
Let's get outta here.

14:39.216 --> 14:41.275
Well, I'm off to serve
food at the soup kitchen.

14:41.276 --> 14:42.510
Now that I lived through this,

14:42.649 --> 14:43.783
I kinda have to keep

14:44.087 --> 14:45.024
a promise I made to someone.

14:45.025 --> 14:45.894
It's God!

14:46.710 --> 14:48.145
Peter, what did you mean?

14:48.146 --> 14:49.207
All right, you want the truth?

14:49.208 --> 14:50.576
They bore the hell outta me, Lois.

14:50.896 --> 14:52.164
Bore the hell outta you?!

14:52.329 --> 14:53.269
They're your kids!

14:53.270 --> 14:54.505
I know, and I love 'em,

14:55.017 --> 14:57.201
but don't you just sometimes
wish they'd run away

14:57.202 --> 14:59.071
or get kidnapped
and be made to work

14:59.076 --> 14:59.949
in a Temple of Doom?

15:04.572 --> 15:06.193
How can you even say that?!

15:06.194 --> 15:07.428
Because, Lois. Meg tells a story

15:07.819 --> 15:09.186
that makes you wanna
blow your brains out,

15:09.192 --> 15:10.444
Stewie just sits there

15:10.445 --> 15:12.114
and Chris is always leaving
his Russian mice around.

15:12.815 --> 15:13.815
Get outta here!

15:13.816 --> 15:15.785
Okay, okay, you don't have to yell.

15:16.187 --> 15:18.371
<i>Let us go find das vaginya.</i>

15:18.372 --> 15:19.307
Listen to you!

15:19.434 --> 15:20.619
You don't know your own kids!

15:20.620 --> 15:21.620
That's the problem!

15:21.872 --> 15:23.428
It's not them, it's you!

15:23.429 --> 15:23.930
Me?!

15:24.056 --> 15:24.990
Yes, you!

15:25.241 --> 15:26.365
And you know what?

15:26.366 --> 15:28.669
You've hurt your kids worse
than any black hole could!

15:28.926 --> 15:30.360
Lois, you're overreacting.

15:30.428 --> 15:31.961
This'll all blow over by tomorrow.

15:36.359 --> 15:37.994
Morning, .

15:38.168 --> 15:38.980
Ha-ha, I'm just kiddin'!

15:38.981 --> 15:40.978
So what do we got, pancakes? Cool!

15:40.979 --> 15:42.914
Hey, what's on tap for
school today, kids?

15:42.915 --> 15:44.549
Shut up, Dad. Whatever.

15:45.226 --> 15:46.294
So, Chris, how, uh,

15:46.474 --> 15:47.787
how are all your friends at school?

15:47.788 --> 15:48.721
What do you care?

15:48.722 --> 15:50.324
You don't know who my friends are.

15:50.658 --> 15:51.663
Sure, I do.

15:51.664 --> 15:54.593
Um, Chandler...

15:54.594 --> 15:56.062
Fonzie...

15:56.593 --> 15:57.827
and Remington Steele?

15:58.403 --> 16:00.275
You got lucky, Dad.

16:00.276 --> 16:02.586
So, Stewie, how's everything
goin' in Lego Land?

16:02.587 --> 16:03.897
Oh, pretty good.
I made a spaceship...

16:03.898 --> 16:05.833
Wait a minute.
I'm not talkin' to you.

16:06.085 --> 16:08.054
Come on, guys. Let's go
eat in the living room.

16:08.081 --> 16:09.481
It stinks in here.

16:10.956 --> 16:12.829
Oh, no, does it stink
'cause I farted?

16:12.830 --> 16:14.462
'Cause sometimes I
can suck 'em back up.

16:14.827 --> 16:16.702
I think we can make up
some of these losses

16:16.703 --> 16:17.837
in the third quarter.

16:21.074 --> 16:21.697
What was that?

16:21.698 --> 16:22.510
What was what?

16:22.511 --> 16:23.711
Oh, nothing.

16:23.882 --> 16:26.386
I thought I smelled a fart,
but now I don't.

16:26.632 --> 16:29.629
They, uh, they're really
pissed at me, aren't they?

16:29.630 --> 16:31.799
Oh, look who's startin' to get it.

16:31.876 --> 16:34.145
Peter, they heard you say
you hate being around them.

16:34.188 --> 16:35.434
They, they know you
have no interest

16:35.435 --> 16:36.312
in getting to know them.

16:36.313 --> 16:37.648
I mean, how-how would you feel?

16:38.058 --> 16:40.360
Well, right now I feel like a jerk.

16:40.369 --> 16:42.272
Peter, if you really do
care about your kids,

16:42.369 --> 16:44.176
you're gonna have to earn back
their respect and affection.

16:44.177 --> 16:45.412
How do I do that?

16:45.929 --> 16:47.465
You gotta spend time with them

16:47.489 --> 16:49.392
and make their interests
your interests.

16:49.988 --> 16:51.991
I guess you're right, Lois.

16:52.047 --> 16:53.421
I'm always screwin' up.

16:53.422 --> 16:55.191
Like that time with Jason Mraz.

16:56.295 --> 16:57.998
Oh, my God! You're Jason Mraz!

16:58.545 --> 16:59.167
No, I'm not.

16:59.168 --> 17:00.478
I'm just some guy with a hat.

17:00.479 --> 17:01.914
Yeah, that's who Jason Mraz is!

17:07.164 --> 17:09.734
Hey, buddy.

17:10.720 --> 17:12.887
What's goin' on?

17:14.094 --> 17:15.530
You having your period?

17:15.531 --> 17:16.340
What?!

17:16.341 --> 17:17.091
I'm just trying

17:17.092 --> 17:18.464
to take an interest
in your interests.

17:18.465 --> 17:19.733
My period's not an interest.

17:20.213 --> 17:21.335
It's something that happens to me

17:21.336 --> 17:22.404
that I cannot control.

17:22.837 --> 17:24.085
Gross.

17:24.086 --> 17:25.708
All right, I'm gonna
go talk to Chris.

17:25.709 --> 17:26.644
Hi, Chris.

17:28.832 --> 17:30.503
Hello... Peter.

17:30.519 --> 17:31.990
You know, I was just thinkin',

17:32.142 --> 17:35.280
when I was your age,
my Uncle Roy shared a beer with me.

17:35.451 --> 17:37.262
I drank it, and I was so excited,
I fell asleep.

17:37.263 --> 17:39.233
I must have tossed and
turned somethin' fierce,

17:40.323 --> 17:42.358
'cause when I woke up,
my pants were off.

17:42.509 --> 17:44.612
Never saw much of
Uncle Roy after that.

17:44.633 --> 17:46.236
Turns out we weren't even related.

17:46.754 --> 17:48.754
Anyway, I thought him sharing
that beer with me was

17:48.755 --> 17:49.956
the coolest thing ever.

17:50.689 --> 17:52.437
And I know nowadays
things are different...

17:52.438 --> 17:53.773
so I got some crystal meth.

17:53.875 --> 17:56.078
I figured we could do it
together as father and son.

17:56.247 --> 17:57.382
I don't know about that.

17:57.434 --> 17:59.002
Tell you what, I'll get us started.

18:01.432 --> 18:05.177
Ah... That feels,
that feels better.

18:05.178 --> 18:06.512
You sure that stuff is okay?

18:06.928 --> 18:09.365
All I know is the guys
who made it are dead.

18:09.738 --> 18:12.342
Why is there no hole in this wall?

18:12.422 --> 18:14.358
You know, this thing is buggin' me.

18:15.856 --> 18:17.689
All right, I'm gonna take a hike.

18:21.479 --> 18:24.084
So you gonna introduce
me to your pals?

18:24.101 --> 18:25.223
That's Trapjaw.

18:25.224 --> 18:26.225
That's Optimus Prime.

18:26.411 --> 18:27.511
That's Destro.

18:27.535 --> 18:28.902
And that's a Care Bear.

18:29.222 --> 18:30.408
You havin' a tea party?

18:30.409 --> 18:32.478
No, we're working out a land deal.

18:32.533 --> 18:34.219
Trapjaw is trying to get a variance

18:34.220 --> 18:36.022
to build an unpermitted
structure within ten feet

18:36.216 --> 18:37.617
of Optimus Prime's property line.

18:38.027 --> 18:39.763
Destro is the City Councilman
who's telling Trapjaw

18:40.402 --> 18:42.397
that he has to file it as
an accessory structure,

18:42.398 --> 18:45.086
and even then it can only be
built at the rear of the lot.

18:45.087 --> 18:47.269
And the Care Bear
is just a Care Bear.

18:47.270 --> 18:49.507
I am so ready!

18:53.953 --> 18:55.988
I don't know, Lois,
I tried my best.

18:56.328 --> 18:58.636
I don't know what else I
possibly could have done.

18:58.637 --> 19:00.508
Peter, you're just gonna
have to do better.

19:00.509 --> 19:02.311
Somehow you've gotta
let those kids know

19:02.320 --> 19:03.723
that they matter to you.

19:03.884 --> 19:05.351
I'll try, Lois.

19:09.564 --> 19:10.812
Kids, come in here!

19:10.813 --> 19:12.515
Your father's got somethin' to say!

19:16.496 --> 19:18.309
Look, I know you
kids ain't too happy

19:18.310 --> 19:19.370
with your dad right now,

19:19.371 --> 19:22.405
but I hope at least you
could see that I'm tryin'.

19:22.866 --> 19:25.967
I mean, I know sometimes we
don't get along with each other.

19:26.239 --> 19:27.426
Hell, if we weren't all related,

19:27.427 --> 19:29.237
this would be like the
worst table at the wedding.

19:29.238 --> 19:30.672
But we're, we're part of a family.

19:31.735 --> 19:33.607
And I'm still your father.

19:33.608 --> 19:35.481
And I promise I love you.

19:35.482 --> 19:39.044
Well, then how come you said you
hated spending time with us?

19:39.045 --> 19:41.480
Look, I may not have said
exactly what I meant.

19:41.539 --> 19:43.788
But I-I can still be your dad

19:43.789 --> 19:46.059
even if we don't have any
of the same interests.

19:46.099 --> 19:48.200
So what do you say,
are we a family again?

19:50.284 --> 19:50.968
I don't buy it.

19:50.969 --> 19:51.655
Me neither.

19:51.656 --> 19:52.841
When you jumped through my ceiling,

19:52.842 --> 19:53.975
you let an owl in.

19:54.217 --> 19:55.403
I know they're supposed to be wise,

19:55.404 --> 19:56.652
but all it did was shriek

19:56.653 --> 19:57.654
and poop out half-digested mice.

19:57.655 --> 19:59.223
Well, then, I guess
ere's only one thing

20:00.277 --> 20:02.179
I can do to regain your love.

20:02.897 --> 20:04.647
Who wants a brand new Xbox?

20:04.648 --> 20:06.483
Yay! Oh, Daddy!

20:06.772 --> 20:09.444
Oh, my God, you're
the best father ever!

20:13.827 --> 20:15.887
Well, I guess if you can't
earn your kids' respect,

20:15.888 --> 20:17.023
you can always buy it.

20:21.133 --> 20:23.704
There's some awesome
stuff in the garbage.

20:30.373 --> 20:31.038
Dad, can we please have
a turn at the Xbox?

20:36.548 --> 20:38.717
uh, now, which one do
I press to shoot now?

20:39.109 --> 20:41.045
Damn it! Ah, crap.

20:41.046 --> 20:42.681
Who's the douchebag
who keeps dyin'?

20:42.983 --> 20:44.583
I'm not a douchebag. I'm new.

20:45.229 --> 20:46.352
Look, if you're no good,

20:46.353 --> 20:47.977
why don't you just
go hide till the end?

20:47.978 --> 20:49.780
All right, I'll go
crouch behind the, uh...

20:50.037 --> 20:50.971
Is this a crouch button?

20:51.910 --> 20:53.658
Ah! Who dropped a grenade?!

20:53.659 --> 20:54.971
Idiot! Learn how to play!

20:54.972 --> 20:56.742
Moron! You suck!

20:56.743 --> 21:57.743
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru